# concept Transformer architecture {#transformer_architecture}

A sequence architecture composing attention, position information, feed-forward transformations, residual paths, and normalization.

# claim Recurrence is not required by the original architecture {#claim_transformer_recurrence}

Evidence: `{#source_vaswani_2017}` and `{#claim_no_recurrence}`. Confidence: high for the original Transformer; later hybrid architectures may reintroduce recurrence.

# claim A Transformer is more than attention alone {#claim_more_than_attention}

Evidence: `{#source_transformer_survey}` and `{#claim_block_composition}`. Confidence: high.

# relates wiki/attention

The mechanism at the center of the architecture.

# relates wiki/scaling

Scaling describes observed behavior as models, data, and compute grow.
